* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
* transmon.qdl - a basic transmon qubit, as a qforge device netlist
*
* The whole circuit is two elements: one Josephson junction, and one big
* capacitor shunting it. Everything that makes a transmon a transmon comes from
* the ratio between them.
*
*     node 1  o--------+--------+
*                      |        |
*                     [X] J1   ===  Csh          J1  : the junction
*                      |        |                Csh : the shunt capacitor
*     node 0  o--------+--------+
*             (ground)
*
* The shunt capacitor is what separates a transmon from a Cooper-pair box. It
* makes the charging energy EC small, so EJ/EC lands in the tens, and the
* qubit's frequency stops depending on the offset charge on the island. The
* price is a small anharmonicity: around -235 MHz here, which is what limits how
* fast a pulse can drive 0->1 without also driving 1->2.
*
* Run it with:
*     qforge --interactive   ->  Design a device  ->  Load a netlist file
*
* or from Python:
*     from qforge.core.device_engine import DeviceEngine
*     device = DeviceEngine().create_device_from_file(
*         "examples/device_files/transmon.qdl"
*     )
*     result = device.analyze()
*     print(result["f01_ghz"], result["anharmonicity_mhz"])
*
* Expected results, for the values below:
*     f01           ~ 4.79 GHz
*     anharmonicity ~ -235 MHz
*     EJ / EC       ~ 71
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

.title  Basic transmon
.name   transmon_example

* Design parameters, written the way a fabricator would specify them. Both are
* named, so either can be swept afterwards without editing this file.
.param  IC   = 30nA              ; junction critical current  -> EJ ~ 14.9 GHz
.param  CSH  = 90fF              ; shunt capacitance          -> EC ~ 0.215 GHz

* Elements.  <name> <node+> <node-> <values...>
J1   1  0   EJ=IC   Cj=2fF       ; the junction, plus its own self-capacitance
Csh  1  0   CSH                  ; the shunt that makes this a transmon

* Bias and basis.
.charge 1 = 0.0                  ; offset charge on the island, in Cooper pairs
.cutoff n1 = 30                  ; charge-basis cutoff; 30 is plenty at this EJ/EC
.levels 6                        ; eigenvalues to compute

.end
